COHORT RETENTION ANALYSIS – INSIGHTS

1. Retention is highest during the first month because this represents the customer's initial purchase activity.

2. Retention generally decreases as the number of months increases, indicating that fewer customers continue purchasing over time.

3. Retention varies across different cohorts, showing differences in customer repeat-purchase behavior.

4. The cohort heatmap makes it easier to identify retention patterns across different signup/purchase months.

5. Cohort analysis can help businesses understand customer retention and identify opportunities to improve repeat purchases and customer engagement.
